[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta\). To find the maximum value of this expression, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 468^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m Let's calculate this value:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 219024} = \sqrt{324000} = 570
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m So the largest possible real part of the given expression is \(570\). Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m a = 324
