[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m = (324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta) + i (336 \cos \theta + 276 \sin \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\), so the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m Let's calculate this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m So the largest possible real part of the expression is \(540\). Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m b = -432
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=798490)[0m # Maximum value of a*cos(theta) + b*sin(theta) is sqrt(a^2 + b^2)
